{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Root-cause evidence (2026-10-31, read-only CI log analysis plus a local simulation; no code changed yet).\n\n1. Windows log, scheduled run 41230936309 (ref 0886e96f03a, after the eastmost-uncheered-nematode stub landed in 688e564ff91), job `sweep (windows)` 124624825616: tests/unit/test_review_bot.py has 84 failing ids. 81 carry the network guard's RuntimeError; 2 are `State object has no attribute 'config'`; 1 is `module 'signal' has no attribute 'SIGKILL'` (test_sigkill_during_a_store_write_orphans_the_mkdir_lock). Run 40797257532 shows the same 84. So the default `_current_revision` stub did not change the Windows result.\n2. Where the RuntimeError escapes: every review-bot traceback is the same chain, before any test code runs: `asyncio.run` -> `events.new_event_loop()` -> `ProactorEventLoop.__init__` -> `_make_self_pipe` -> `socket.socketpair()` -> `socket._fallback_socketpair` -> `csock.connect(('127.0.0.1', port))` -> tests/conftest.py `_guard_socket_connect` raises. Windows has no AF_UNIX socketpair, so the stdlib builds the event loop's self-pipe from an AF_INET loopback pair inside the process, and the guard blocks every AF_INET connect. TestClient/lifespan tests reach the same path through their event loop. Across the whole run, 364 of 366 network-guard tracebacks contain `_fallback_socketpair` (the 2 others are in test_interpret_failure_seam.py and test_engine_dir.py).\n3. Local reproduction on macOS (Python 3.12.14): a scratch pytest plugin sets `socket.socketpair = socket._fallback_socketpair`, which is what Windows uses. tests/unit/test_review_bot.py: 130 passed without it; 83 failed, 47 passed with it. The 83 are exactly the Windows failures minus the SIGKILL test (set comparison: 0 extra, 1 missing = SIGKILL). The 6 named tests (the drain, drain-bounded, in-flight store write, gerrit webhook peer, voter malformed event, and the 782aa2921f6 cancel-bounded test) all fail with the plugin and pass without it.\n4. Prior intent: commit 5697f2e1117 narrowed the guard to AF_INET/AF_INET6 so that local IPC (AF_UNIX) passes; its stated rule is that local IPC never touches the network. The in-process loopback socketpair is the Windows form of the same local IPC."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793500187767261001,"uuid":"3935cb50-71ae-4055-9588-f137f4a15185"}